// Title: Root Certificate Installed From Susp Locations
// Sigma ID: 5f6a601c-2ecb-498b-9c33-660362323afa
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2022-09-09 | Modified: 2023-01-16
// ATT&CK: defense-impairment, T1553.004
// Description: Adversaries may install a root certificate on a compromised system to avoid warnings when
//   connecting to adversary controlled web servers.
// False positives:
//   - Unlikely
// References:
//   - https://www.microsoft.com/security/blog/2022/09/07/profiling-dev-0270-phosphorus-ransomware-operations/
//   - https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/powershell/module/pki/import-certificate?view=windowsserver2022-ps
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_powershell_import_cert_susp_locations.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, microsoft_xdr schema)

DeviceProcessEvents
| where (ProcessCommandLine contains "Import-Certificate" and ProcessCommandLine contains " -FilePath " and ProcessCommandLine contains "Cert:\\LocalMachine\\Root") and (ProcessCommandLine contains "\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\" or ProcessCommandLine contains ":\\Windows\\TEMP\\" or ProcessCommandLine contains "\\Desktop\\" or ProcessCommandLine contains "\\Downloads\\" or ProcessCommandLine contains "\\Perflogs\\" or ProcessCommandLine contains ":\\Users\\Public\\")
